 ],
 "literal": "Strong-charioted Naḷḷi's forest cowherds' / many cows yielded ghee-like Toṇṭi's / entirely matured white paddy's hot cooked rice, / even if offered in seven vessels, is small, my friend, / for the distress that made large shoulders thin, / the offering to the crow that cawed for the guest to arrive!",
 "translation": "Even if we offer hot cooked rice made from white paddy grown fully in Toṇṭi—a town rich in ghee yielded by the many cows of the cowherds in the forest of Naḷḷi who has a strong chariot—piled high in seven large vessels, it would still be too small an offering for the crow that cawed to announce the arrival of our guest, which cured the distress that made your large shoulders waste away, my friend!",
 "modern": "வலிமையான தேரையுடைய நள்ளியின் காட்டுப் பகுதியில் வாழும் இடையர்களின் பல பசுக்கள் தந்த நெய்யைப் போன்ற வளமிக்க தொண்டி நகரில் முழுமையாக விளைந்த வெண்ணெல்லின் சூடான சோற்றை, ஏழு கலங்களில் நிறைத்து வைத்தாலும் அது சிறியதே ஆகும், என் தோழியே! உன்னுடைய பெரிய தோள்களை மெலியச் செய்த துன்பத்தைப் போக்கும் வகையில், நம் தலைவர் விருந்தினராக வருவதைக் கரைந்து அறிவித்த காக்கைக்கு நாம் அளிக்கும் பலி உணவு அது.",
 "explanation": "This poem is set in the Mullai (forest) landscape, which is associated with patient waiting and the return of the hero. The speaker is the heroine's friend, addressing the heroine upon the hero's return. The heroine had been wasting away in grief during the hero's absence, causing her beautiful, large shoulders to grow thin. A crow cawed, traditionally signaling the arrival of a guest, and indeed, the hero returned, curing her distress. In gratitude, the friend declares that even an immense offering of the finest hot rice from the fertile town of Tondi, served in seven huge vessels, is too small a reward for that auspicious crow. The imagery of Tondi's rich ghee and white paddy highlights the abundance and joy that returns to the household with the hero.",
